  grid 1 (scene 1) [street] EXT. quiet neighbourhood street — NIGHT
    1. Baker stands behind the workbench inside the shop glowing along the quiet street beneath a blue, sunless sky.
    2. Baker sets a ball of dough on the workbench nearest us.
  grid 2 (scene 2) [shop] INT. shop — CONTINUOUS
    1. Baker presses the folded dough away from us with both palms.
    2. Baker shapes the dough into a loaf beside a tray of plump croissants.
    3. Baker lifts the loaf from the workbench beside the open oven.
    4. Baker slides the loaf into the oven to the left of the workbench.
    5. Baker slides the pastry tray of croissants into the oven, away from us.
    6. Baker closes the oven door.
  grid 3 (scene 3) [shop] INT. shop — LATER
    1. Morning light brightens the shop's front window.
    2. Baker pulls the oven door down toward us as steam rolls out of the opening.
    3. Baker draws a golden loaf and a tray of deeply browned croissants out of the oven with thick mitts.
    4. Baker sets the croissant tray on the wooden workbench while keeping the loaf in one mitt.
    5. Baker lowers the loaf onto the wire cooling rack as tiny cracks open in its crust.
  grid 4 (scene 4) [shop] INT. blue front door — CONTINUOUS
    1. Baker turns the strip beneath the door-mounted shop name sign to OPEN.
    2. Neighbour steps through the blue front doorway toward us, carrying a canvas shopping bag.
    3. Parent follows neighbour inside holding child's hand as child looks past baker toward the croissants on the workbench.
    4. Child smiles at the croissants.
  grid 5 (scene 5) [shop] INT. counter — CONTINUOUS
    1. Baker lifts a croissant from the workbench tray while neighbour, parent and child wait across the counter.
    2. Baker slips the croissant into a paper bag on the counter.
    3. Baker passes the paper bag across the counter into neighbour's hand.
    4. Baker lifts the loaf from the cooling rack.
    5. Baker folds paper around the loaf on the counter.
    6. Baker's shoulders droop beneath the apron straps as parent receives the wrapped loaf.
    7. Neighbour and parent smile at baker, parent holding the wrapped loaf.
    8. Baker lifts their head and smiles with widening eyes.
  grid 6 (scene 6) [street] EXT. quiet neighbourhood street — DAY
    1. Sunlight illuminates the door-mounted shop sign bearing the name “The Corner Oven.”
    2. The words “Come in. Your morning starts here.” appear beneath the shop name.
